{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And if the man has no kinsman.</b> The claimant whom he had made swear died, and he has no heirs." "<b>To restore the guilt-offering to him.</b> When this one reconsidered to confess his sin. And our Sages said: Is there any person in Israel who has no kinsman — either a son, or a brother, or close flesh of his father's family, tracing upward as far as Jacob? Rather, this is the convert who died and has no heirs (Sanhedrin 68b)." "<b>The guilt-offering that is restored.</b> This is the principal and the fifth (Bava Kamma 110a)." "<b>To YHWH, to the priest.</b> HaShem acquired it and gave it to the priest of that watch (Sifrei)." "<b>Besides the ram of atonement.</b> The one stated in Leviticus, which he must bring."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:27.735779136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}